blocks.en:
All methods share the same BM25 retriever; they differ only in how LLM-generated text is used to bridge the query–corpus vocabulary gap. We compare MERGE against three published LLM-based expansion baselines and a no-APO ablation:
(i) Vanilla BM25 : the original query with no expansion, the reference point;
(ii) docT5query ( Nogueira and Lin, 2019 ) : a supervised, corpus-dependent baseline that fine-tunes T5 on MS MARCO (document, query) pairs so it can predict queries from documents, then runs T5 on every document in the corpus and appends the predicted queries to that document in the BM25 index—the LLM’s input is documents;
(iii) BM25+Exp4Fuse ( Liu and Zhang, 2025 ) : an unsupervised, query-only baseline that runs two BM25 passes (over the original query and over an LLM-produced pseudo-document generated from the user query) and combines the two ranked lists with a modified reciprocal-rank fusion;
(iv) docT5query+Exp4Fuse ( Liu and Zhang, 2025 ; Nogueira and Lin, 2019 ) : the stronger baseline reported by the Exp4Fuse paper, stacking (ii) and (iii);
(v) MERGE w/o APO : MERGE with the same two-stage architecture but using only the hand-crafted seed prompts, to isolate the effect of prompt optimization.
Like Exp4Fuse variants and unlike docT5query, MERGE takes only the user query as input to its LLMs; unlike Exp4Fuse variants, MERGE issues a single BM25 pass with no rank fusion.

blocks.zh:
所有方法都共享相同的BM25检索器;它们仅在如何使用LLM生成的文本来弥补查询-corpus词汇差距上有所不同. 我们比较了MERGE和三个公布的基于LLM的扩展基线和无APO的扩展:
(一) 香草BM25:没有扩展的原始查询,参考点;
(二) docT5query(Nogueira和Lin, 2019年):一个有监督的、依赖实体的基线,对MS MARCO(文件、查询)上的T5进行微调,以便它能预测文件的查询,然后在书目中的每一份文件上运行T5,并在BM25索引中将预测的查询附于该文件 -- -- LLM的投入是文件;
(三)BM25+Exp4Fuse(刘和章,2025年):一个无监督的,仅限查询的基线,运行两个BM25通道(在原查询之上,在用户查询生成的LLM制成的伪文件之上),并将两个排名列表与修改的对等排名组合合并;
(四) docT5query+Exp4Fuse(刘和章,2025年;Nogueira和林,2019年):Exp4Fuse纸张报告的较强基线,堆叠(二)和(三);
(五) MERGE w/o APO : MERGE 具有相同的两阶段架构,但只使用手工制作的种子提示,以隔离即时优化的效果.
类似Exp4Fuse变体和与Doc不同 T5query,MERGE只将用户查询作为对其LLMS的输入;与Exp4Fuse变体不同的是,MERGE发行了单个BM25的传球,没有等级组合.
